---
description: Quality, accessibility, performance and security requirements
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md`.

- Validate server-side form input; never trust client validation alone.
- Keep API keys and email provider tokens in Cloudflare secrets or equivalent server-side environment storage.
- Avoid logging message bodies, email addresses or other submitted personal data.
- Use spam protection and rate limiting as appropriate for a public form; handle errors without leaking internals.
- Maintain semantic headings, labelled inputs, accessible status messages, keyboard focus and responsive layout.
- Prefer lightweight static output, optimised images and minimal third-party scripts.
- Run `bash scripts/ai-checks.sh` when available; state what passed, failed or was skipped.
- Inspect `git diff` and avoid unrelated changes.
- Do not commit, push, merge or delete branches without permission.
